30
00:11:09,539 --> 00:11:14,659
As you know, sentences and paragraphs are not just strung together

31
00:11:14,659 --> 00:11:15,779
one after the other.

32
00:11:15,879 --> 00:11:20,279
The ideas they express both within and between sentences are connected

33
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:25,700
by means of various words and phrases that relate the ideas to each other.

34
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:31,820
And, you know, we have connectors like and, but, or, yet.

35
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:38,080
However, therefore, these are the connectors that we most frequently use

36
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:41,299
to connect the ideas that we use in a text.

37
00:11:41,299 --> 00:11:51,720
And, but these are not only the words or language structures that we use to connect

38
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:56,720
or maybe achieve coherence or unity in the text.

39
00:11:56,720 --> 00:12:02,360
There are other items in English that have the property of reference.

40
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:10,200
That is, they do not have meaning themselves, but they refer to something else for their meaning.

41
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:15,839
And to identify, to be able to identify these reference words

42
00:12:15,839 --> 00:12:22,319
actually helps you to improve your reading speed and comprehension

43
00:12:22,319 --> 00:12:27,100
in your English lessons.

44
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:28,600
So what are they?

45
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,879
What are the reference words?

46
00:12:30,879 --> 00:12:35,299
These are the words or phrases that substitute for other words or phrases.

47
00:12:36,079 --> 00:12:41,440
They usually refer back to ideas that have already been expressed,

48
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:45,159
but they occasionally refer forward.

49
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:50,159
They sometimes also refer forward to ideas yet to be stated.

50
00:12:50,539 --> 00:12:50,700
Okay.

51
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:56,079
So when you see a reference words like it, them, him, her, whatever,

52
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,799
you generally look back.

53
00:12:57,799 --> 00:13:03,660
I mean, look at the previous sentence to be able to find what it refers to.

54
00:13:04,019 --> 00:13:10,860
But sometimes, very occasionally, they might refer to an item,

55
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:17,220
a language item, a pronoun coming after the reference word.

